# Sentinel Ultra — Reviewer Workflow

Peer ECs verify submitter work. Reach an **independent** task assessment, then pick a review outcome.

## Review outcomes

| Outcome | When |
|---------|------|
| **Accept** | Accurate, complete, well-supported; task meets Ultra bar after any fixes |
| **Needs Revision** | Authoring errors remain (instruction/tests/oracle/bundle) that submitter can still fix |
| **Reject** | Only after **maximum revisions** reached and work still inadequate. Not a substitute for Needs Revision |

If platform shows "Maximum Revisions Reached", use Reject (or Accept + adjudicator notes if Reject unavailable).

## By submitter path

**Valid as-is:** Repeat content review; confirm instruction↔tests↔oracle↔PR; metadata sane; no hidden scope drift.

**Fixable:** Confirm rewrites fix reported issues; no new leakage/hidden requirements; PR only expanded not reduced; upload is full flat task bundle; cite `runs/` when relevant.

**Not Fixable:** Confirm issues are real and match Not Fixable categories (PR scope reduce/replace, or disallowed env).

## Reviewer form

- Verdict: Accept / Needs Revision / Reject
- On Accept: confirm Ultra checklist (coverage, faithfulness, no LLM tone, no leakage, oracle match, not over-prescriptive)
- On Needs Revision: tag error categories (Instruction Styling/Prescriptiveness, Test↔Instruction Misalignment, Coverage, Hints/Answers, Oracle, PR Scope Violation, Environment, etc.) + concrete revision notes citing guideline sections
- Acknowledge submitter Comments / rebuttal
- **Submission Quality Score 1–5** (1–2 → Needs Revision; 3–5 → Accept)

## Local Harbor for reviewers

Not required. Optional if it helps verify a finding. Prefer document/logic review of uploaded artifacts and eval reports.

## Do not

- Use old Accept/Reject-only model without Needs Revision
- Reject when Needs Revision is still available
- Ignore Comments for Reviewer
- Mark Not Fixable for infra/platform flakes (rate limits, blank feedback)
